heater.description:
The heating rod connects by WLAN/LAN to the MQTT broker of Home Assistant and is searched there.

{status}

**Not found?** Set up MQTT in the heating rod: connect to its hotspot “novolto-xxxxxx”, open http://192.168.2.1/expert (or in the home network http://IP-of-the-rod/expert), set `mqtt.broker_uri` = `mqtt://HA-IP:1883`, user and password of a Home Assistant user, restart (HA-IP = address of Home Assistant). Then tick “Search again”.

bsb.description:
Searches BSB adapters: ESPHome devices with BSB values or the action `bsb_get` (e.g. BSB-Atom), BSB-LAN from the Home Assistant integration “BSB-LAN” and optionally in the home network.

{status}

After setup the controller is detected automatically (parameters 6224–6226). Parameter scan, bus polling and bus log are in the panel under **EMS-Regelung → ESP-Bus-Adapter**.
